  "id": "COMPOUND:22897 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Myxotyroside B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the activation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through a series of interconnected targets. The evidence suggests that Myxotyroside B directly targets VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of (2E)-2-[(5S,6R,10S)-10-hydroxy-6-(3-hydroxypropyl)-4-methoxy-10-methyl-3-[(3Z,5E)-11-methyl-7-methylidenedodeca-3,5,10-trien-3-yl]spiro[4.5]decan-7-ylidene]propanal, a compound that ultimately has a target of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This indicates a potential mechanism where Myxotyroside B may influence the activity of LC-PTP through a chain of molecular interactions involving VMRC-LCP and the aforementioned compound. The evidence supports a pathway where Myxotyroside B's effects are mediated through VMRC-LCP and a related metabolite, ultimately leading to the regulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Myxotyroside B in modulating the activity of this phosphatase, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
